<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Choe Chiwon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 857</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Ch'oe Ch'i-won</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Choe Chiwon was a scholar and poet of late Silla. Sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> as a boy, he passed the Tang civil service examination and served there, writing a famous proclamation against the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huang-chao">Huang Chao</a>. He returned to Silla in 885 but, frustrated by the rigid bone-rank system and the kingdom's decline, withdrew to the mountains. He is honoured as a founder of Korean literature in Chinese.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/choe-chiwon.jpg" alt="Choe Chiwon" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Choi_Chi-won.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
